<title>USA: AFSALA Bancorp sets buy back plan.</title>
<headline>AFSALA Bancorp sets buy back plan.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM, N.Y. 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>AFSALA Bancorp Inc said it plans to buy back up to 72,737 shares, or 5 percent, of its common stock in the open market.</p>
<p>The company, which is the parent holding company of Amsterdam Federal Bank, currently has 1,454,750 common shares outstanding.</p>
<p>President and Chief Executive John Lisicki said in a statement that the repurchase plan would be used to mitigate some of the potentially dilutive effets of its stock benefit plans as well as for general corporate purposes.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
